A||N||2||Cozmo||Very slight miss at neutral throttle...why???||||5||
Z||000000||Cozmo||07-03-2001||05:46 PM||||OK, the '85 2M6 targa engine now has 1K miles since the top end was rebuilt.  It starts and runs great with no codes or weirdness...<BR>BUT...<BR>When it's in fourth gear at about 3K RPM with "dead" throttle (neither accelerating or decelerating) it has a very slight "boink" (yeah, I know, real technical term  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ).  It'll go RRRRRRRRRboinkRRRRRRboink etc.<BR> If you go faster or slower it goes away and is not noticable at any other time.<BR>I've got all new stuff, but I tried swapping out some stuff (dist., coil, plugs & wires etc.) with no change.<BR>Vacuum is 30, fuel press. is 45, idle 1K, timing set by the book.  New fuel pump and filter.<BR>Like I said, it doesn't affect the performance but it's irritating and if it's anything bad I want to "nip it in the bud" so to speak.<BR>Does anyone have any ideas about what this could be or maybe some way to troubleshoot or isolate it?  I did some searches, but this is a real "vague" problem and what I've found and tried didn't fix it.<BR>Thanks A LOT, I just want all Forum members to know how much I appreciate this place and especially Cliff's efforts...<BR>C02M0||||reg||5
Z||000001||PBJ||07-03-2001||09:33 PM||||I see you said you tried swapping plug wires but - did you try a complete new set.  An intermittent "miss" has got to be due to secondary ignition failure and is most commonly due to bad spark plug wire.  Than may want to remove those plugs and check for fouling or gap concern.<P>hope this helps.||||reg||1
Z||000002||MrPBody||07-04-2001||10:05 AM||||This may or may not be relevant . . .<P>My wife's '88 Cherokee 4.0 had a similar irregular misfire at cruising throttle.  The problem was distributor rotor phasing: the engine management system advances the spark timing at light load, so much that the spark happens before the rotor points to the distributor cap terminal.  This is a known Jeep 4.0 problem; the official fix is to cut-off the distributor locating tab, and rotate the distributor slightly.<P>Plausible?<BR>||||reg||1
